          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "The main unfinished task is **closing the global coverage gap in Stage 4**. The latest work completes several finite steps that were still prospective when overview 02 was written.\n\n| Stage | Current status and remaining work |\n|---|---|\n| **0–1: baseline and evaluator** | Complete. Manuscript baseline, evaluator, error accounting, and finite validation are established. |\n| **2: performance comparison** | Completed, but the required twofold speed advantage was **not achieved**. Reopening this needs a materially improved method; further height scans alone are not justified. |\n| **3: analytic estimates** | Finite signed inequalities and effective arithmetic-tail estimates are proved and replayed. What remains is a sufficiently strong signed estimate or exterior exclusion for the uncovered region. |\n| **4: global consumer** | **Still open.** Assemble a complete slab or canopy argument with certified coverage, margins, endpoints, and feasible computational cost. |\n| **5: final closure** | Existing finite certificates have passed replay. The eventual global package still needs full replay, a complete claim ledger, and integration into the manuscript and research summaries. |\n\nThe precise gap for the current slab route is\n\n\\[\nt\\in[0.01,0.2],\\qquad 1001<|x|<e^{6400}.\n\\]\n\nThe central rectangle through \\(|x|=1001\\) is covered; the inherited uniform exterior exclusion starts at \\(e^{6400}\\). Closing this requires an improved exterior threshold with feasible intervening certification, an analytic argument across the gap, or a fully assembled alternative canopy route.\n\nNotes 11–13 already supply explicit tail constants and onset, bounded retained-evaluation costs, a certified vertical wall, and finite-height collision exclusion. Those tasks should **not** be restarted. The next research priority is determining which global route can actually close the remaining region. **No new Newman bound follows yet.**\n\nThe detailed status is recorded in the [progress tracker](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-3/11_arithmetic_collision_rigidity/research-progress/02_UPDATED_RESEARCH_PLAN_PROGRESS_20261018.md) and [latest coverage ledger](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-3/11_arithmetic_collision_rigidity/numerics/high_height_consumer/HIGH_HEIGHT_CONSUMER_LEDGER_20261018.json)."
